Revision history for Data-Coloured

{{$NEXT}}
  - The internal knowledge base of the repository states the Unicode rule as
    the decision in force: the UTF-8 flag of a string decides the unit of its
    rendering, an unflagged string stays a byte stream.
  - The release tarball no longer carries the agent files of the repository,
    the .claude directory and the worktree marker are out of it. CLAUDE.md
    stays, it describes the architecture of the distribution.
  - The POD of Data::Coloured, DDC and the ddc script carries one SUPPORT
    section, generated by the bundle, with the issue tracker and the IRC
    channel.
  - Data::Coloured and DDC document the four exported functions coloured,
    poloured, pc and c with a section of their own, so the POD names what a
    caller gets.
  - A call with more than one argument renders all of them, so
    coloured('a','b') shows "ab". Every argument keeps its own unit, a byte
    argument next to an argument with characters still shows its bytes as
    <ff>.
  - A multi-byte UTF-8 character is now rendered from its UTF-8 bytes instead
    of its code point, so "ä" shows up as <c3a4> and not as <e4>.
  - The distribution builds from the source tree and ships the Perl 5 licence
    as a committed LICENSE file.
  - README.md documents the module, its two export tiers and all four functions.
  - Continuous integration runs on GitHub Actions for Perl 5.36, 5.38 and 5.40.
  - Declare the runtime dependencies Term::ANSIColor and Exporter in the
    cpanfile, so the distribution installs its dependencies automatically.
  - DDC exports all four functions coloured, poloured, pc and c, so a script
    that imports DDC gets the complete API of Data::Coloured.
  - The ddc script shows its usage for --help and -h on STDOUT, reports an
    unknown option, a missing file and a closed standard input on STDERR
    and exits with 2, 1 and 1, so a broken command line is told apart from
    a successful run.
